/**
 * News' port, slice 1 (zeff-plugins/plugins/news-ext): the heart of the sync — the feeds fetched, their items read, what is new kept, everything scored for
 * you. The lambda `news.round` (the built-in's fetch part of syncNews and addItems: sources due, conditional GET, the feed reader, what is new against what is
 * kept and what was cleared away), the lambda `news.rescore` (the built-in's own scoring — interests, mutes, what you liked, your todos and profile, the sources you
 * trust) hand back statements; the flow `news.fetch-round` writes them (sql.exec) over the plugin's stores, which ADOPT the built-in's tables (news_sources,
 * news_items, news_gone, news_terms, news_similar — nothing copied). The pure cores are bundled from scripts/port-news/core/core.ts.
 *
 * Slice 2 added what you do (news.act: read, save, hide, vote, seen, sources, forget) and the clearing away at the end of a round. Not yet (still the built-in's): the agent's funnel, reading ahead, the tags (corpus and AI), the
 * overview (digest), the discovery of feeds, the taste and "more like this", the actions on an item (read, save, hide, vote), the page and its settings.
 *
 *   npx tsx scripts/port-news.mts [<zeff-plugins folder>]     (default ../zeff-plugins)
 */
